      "side": 1,
      "message": "The patch looks correct to me, however I am a bit concerned about the usage of the `rcu_read_lock_any_held()` API from the `fs/` code. This API was originally intended for lockdep checks and not as a reliable way for checking for existence of RCU readers.\n\nIIRC, we `return 1;` from those `rcu*held*` functions simply because without lockdep enabled, those checks are unused anyway and perhaps (IIRC) there is a reason like the warnings need to be silenced always even if the rcu*held functions disagree.\n\nWe should discuss this more upstream. In particular, the `fs/` code checking for \"atomicity\" using `rcu_read_lock_any_held()` does not fully make sense to me, because preemptible RCU\u0027s read-side critical sections are not atomic.\n\nFor posting upstream, you could CC `rcu@vger.kernel.org` which will go out to the others in the RCU team and me.",
      "revId": "033e21be9cfd101f27faf70adda5319ebfe253f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
